o['context']['explanation']+=' Startup reconstructs log bounds and configuration from caller Storage, loads saved term/vote/commit and becomes follower. Snapshot restoration rejects obsolete or ineligible snapshots, fast-forwards a matching committed boundary, or installs snapshot history and configuration; a pending snapshot prevents promotion. Configuration activation uses validated simple changes or joint enter/leave, preserves progress for retained peers, initializes new progress at zero and handles configured leader removal. Application progress can initiate automatic joint exit.'
o['context']['behavior_ids']+=['B_RECONSTRUCT','B_CONFIG']
o['context']['source_ids']+=['src_startup','src_snapshot_restore','src_changer','src_restore_config','src_log_recover','src_applied']
o['connection']['explanation']='Term/role reset discards votes, peer progress and safe-read acknowledgment tracker while preserving local log and committed frontier. Self progress is initialized from local lastIndex, including potentially unstable inherited entries, so Match must not be equated with a fresh durable acknowledgment. Leader formation appends a current-term empty entry; commit requires the selected entry term to equal the leader term, preventing the old self frontier alone from authorizing new-term commitment. Active membership changes reinterpret retained progress and can re-evaluate commit; new peers begin Match=0. Stale-term replies do not advance leader support or stabilize entries. Local append completion additionally matches entry term/index; a later current-term append message can reconfirm outstanding writes. Committed state and application acknowledgments survive term changes: apply responses are term zero, snapshot completion can be processed despite stale term, and applied uses a monotonic maximum. Pending pre-commit read requests survive reset but enter the new read-only mechanism only after current-term commitment; existing safe-read acknowledgment state is reset. Recovery starts as follower with caller-supplied persisted prefix and configuration, not restored leadership.'
